UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇧🇪 Belgium — mandatory B2B e-invoicing via Peppol</h3><p>Structured e-invoicing is now mandatory for domestic B2B transactions between Belgian VAT-registered businesses, using Peppol BIS Billing 3.0 / EN 16931. PDF and paper invoices no longer qualify as of today. A three-month administrative tolerance period runs until 1 April, after which a progressive penalty regime (€1,500 / €3,000 / €5,000 per infraction) applies — so this window is genuinely worth using to close any remaining gaps, not just to wait it out.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-01-01-belgium-mandatory-b2b-peppol';
UPDATE story_translations SET html = '<h3>🇧🇪 Belgium — mandatory B2B e-invoicing via Peppol</h3><p>Structured e-invoicing is now mandatory for domestic B2B transactions between Belgian VAT-registered businesses, using Peppol BIS Billing 3.0 / EN 16931. PDF and paper invoices no longer qualify as of today. A three-month administrative tolerance period runs until 1 April, after which a progressive penalty regime (€1,500 / €3,000 / €5,000 per infraction) applies — so this window is genuinely worth using to close any remaining gaps, not just to wait it out.</p>' WHERE story_id = '2026-01-01-belgium-mandatory-b2b-peppol' AND lang = 'en';
UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇲🇾 Malaysia — MyInvois Phase 4 begins</h3><p>Businesses with annual turnover between RM1 million and RM5 million enter the mandate today, with a relaxation period on submission-error penalties running through to the end of 2027. Individual e-invoices above RM10,000 are now mandatory — consolidated invoicing is no longer permitted for amounts at that level.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-01-01-malaysia-myinvois-phase-4';
UPDATE story_translations SET html = '<h3>🇲🇾 Malaysia — MyInvois Phase 4 begins</h3><p>Businesses with annual turnover between RM1 million and RM5 million enter the mandate today, with a relaxation period on submission-error penalties running through to the end of 2027. Individual e-invoices above RM10,000 are now mandatory — consolidated invoicing is no longer permitted for amounts at that level.</p>' WHERE story_id = '2026-01-01-malaysia-myinvois-phase-4' AND lang = 'en';
UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇧🇷 Brazil — CBS/IBS test fields required</h3><p>As Brazil''s dual-VAT reform begins, electronic tax documents (NF-e, NFC-e, NFS-e) must now include the new CBS and IBS fields at test rates of 0.9% and 0.1% respectively. There''s no financial impact yet at these test rates, but the legal obligation to include the data correctly already applies — and validation tightens considerably from April.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-01-01-brazil-cbs-ibs-test-fields';
UPDATE story_translations SET html = '<h3>🇧🇷 Brazil — CBS/IBS test fields required</h3><p>As Brazil''s dual-VAT reform begins, electronic tax documents (NF-e, NFC-e, NFS-e) must now include the new CBS and IBS fields at test rates of 0.9% and 0.1% respectively. There''s no financial impact yet at these test rates, but the legal obligation to include the data correctly already applies — and validation tightens considerably from April.</p>' WHERE story_id = '2026-01-01-brazil-cbs-ibs-test-fields' AND lang = 'en';
UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇲🇽 Mexico — 2026 tax reform takes effect</h3><p>SAT''s enforcement powers strengthen from today, adding stricter authenticity checks and — notably — new criminal liability for false or simulated CFDIs. This is a meaningful escalation from the previous purely administrative penalty framework. Worth reviewing your defense documentation and cancellation procedures now, given SAT can request supporting evidence within just 5 business days.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-01-01-mexico-2026-tax-reform';
UPDATE story_translations SET html = '<h3>🇲🇽 Mexico — 2026 tax reform takes effect</h3><p>SAT''s enforcement powers strengthen from today, adding stricter authenticity checks and — notably — new criminal liability for false or simulated CFDIs. This is a meaningful escalation from the previous purely administrative penalty framework. Worth reviewing your defense documentation and cancellation procedures now, given SAT can request supporting evidence within just 5 business days.</p>' WHERE story_id = '2026-01-01-mexico-2026-tax-reform' AND lang = 'en';
UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇳🇿 New Zealand — high-volume government agencies must send and receive e-invoices</h3><p>Agencies processing more than 2,000 domestic trade invoices annually must now be fully capable of both sending and receiving structured e-invoices — using the PINT A-NZ format, mandatory for government e-invoicing since May 2025 — and must pay 95% of them within 5 business days. If you supply an agency at this volume, this is the moment payment terms should actually start improving.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-01-01-new-zealand-agency-einvoicing';
UPDATE story_translations SET html = '<h3>🇳🇿 New Zealand — high-volume government agencies must send and receive e-invoices</h3><p>Agencies processing more than 2,000 domestic trade invoices annually must now be fully capable of both sending and receiving structured e-invoices — using the PINT A-NZ format, mandatory for government e-invoicing since May 2025 — and must pay 95% of them within 5 business days. If you supply an agency at this volume, this is the moment payment terms should actually start improving.</p>' WHERE story_id = '2026-01-01-new-zealand-agency-einvoicing' AND lang = 'en';
UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇭🇷 Croatia — Fiskalizacija 2.0 goes live</h3><p>Croatia''s biggest e-invoicing reform yet: structured issuance, receipt, and real-time e-reporting are now mandatory for all VAT-registered, Croatian-established taxpayers — layered on top of the B2G mandate already in force since 2019. This includes a 5-day buyer-side fiscalization workflow and monthly e-reporting by the 20th of each month, plus an 11-year archiving requirement for original XML invoices.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you operate in any of these six markets, this is the moment to confirm — not assume — that whatever went live over the holidays is actually working correctly in production, not just configured and left untested.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-01-01-croatia-fiskalizacija-2';
UPDATE story_translations SET html = '<h3>🇭🇷 Croatia — Fiskalizacija 2.0 goes live</h3><p>Croatia''s biggest e-invoicing reform yet: structured issuance, receipt, and real-time e-reporting are now mandatory for all VAT-registered, Croatian-established taxpayers — layered on top of the B2G mandate already in force since 2019. This includes a 5-day buyer-side fiscalization workflow and monthly e-reporting by the 20th of each month, plus an 11-year archiving requirement for original XML invoices.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you operate in any of these six markets, this is the moment to confirm — not assume — that whatever went live over the holidays is actually working correctly in production, not just configured and left untested.</p>' WHERE story_id = '2026-01-01-croatia-fiskalizacija-2' AND lang = 'en';
UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇵🇱 Poland — KSeF mandatory for large taxpayers</h3><p>Large taxpayers with turnover above PLN 200 million became the first group required to issue B2B invoices through the Krajowy System e-Faktur (KSeF) clearance platform today. This is a genuine clearance model — an invoice carries no legal effect until KSeF has validated and cleared it, using the FA(3) XML schema submitted via API. Everyone else follows in April, and micro-entrepreneurs from January 2027; Poland is deliberately phasing this in by taxpayer size rather than switching on all at once, which is worth knowing if you''re a smaller business assuming you''re already in scope.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you''re a large Polish taxpayer, this is no longer a planning exercise. Confirm your API integration with KSeF is actually live, and that staff and any third-party issuer authorisations are properly configured — a misconfigured authorisation is one of the more common reasons clearance fails silently in the first weeks.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-02-01-poland-ksef-large-taxpayers';
UPDATE story_translations SET html = '<h3>🇵🇱 Poland — KSeF mandatory for large taxpayers</h3><p>Large taxpayers with turnover above PLN 200 million became the first group required to issue B2B invoices through the Krajowy System e-Faktur (KSeF) clearance platform today. This is a genuine clearance model — an invoice carries no legal effect until KSeF has validated and cleared it, using the FA(3) XML schema submitted via API. Everyone else follows in April, and micro-entrepreneurs from January 2027; Poland is deliberately phasing this in by taxpayer size rather than switching on all at once, which is worth knowing if you''re a smaller business assuming you''re already in scope.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you''re a large Polish taxpayer, this is no longer a planning exercise. Confirm your API integration with KSeF is actually live, and that staff and any third-party issuer authorisations are properly configured — a misconfigured authorisation is one of the more common reasons clearance fails silently in the first weeks.</p>' WHERE story_id = '2026-02-01-poland-ksef-large-taxpayers' AND lang = 'en';
UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇸🇦 Saudi Arabia — ZATCA Fatoora Wave 23</h3><p>Businesses with VAT-taxable turnover above SAR 750,000 in 2022, 2023, or 2024 were required to complete Phase 2 integration with the Fatoora platform for real-time clearance from today — meaning invoices carry a UUID, QR code, and cryptographic stamp, submitted via API for real-time B2B/B2G clearance. ZATCA continues its wave-based rollout — Wave 24 follows in June, dropping the threshold to SAR 375,000 and bringing in nearly every VAT-registered business in the country.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if your turnover crossed SAR 750,000 in any of those three reference years, assume you''re in Wave 23 unless ZATCA has told you otherwise — direct notification typically arrives around six months ahead, so if you haven''t heard anything and think you should have, it''s worth checking proactively rather than waiting for a letter that may already be delayed.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-03-01-saudi-arabia-zatca-wave-23';
UPDATE story_translations SET html = '<h3>🇸🇦 Saudi Arabia — ZATCA Fatoora Wave 23</h3><p>Businesses with VAT-taxable turnover above SAR 750,000 in 2022, 2023, or 2024 were required to complete Phase 2 integration with the Fatoora platform for real-time clearance from today — meaning invoices carry a UUID, QR code, and cryptographic stamp, submitted via API for real-time B2B/B2G clearance. ZATCA continues its wave-based rollout — Wave 24 follows in June, dropping the threshold to SAR 375,000 and bringing in nearly every VAT-registered business in the country.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if your turnover crossed SAR 750,000 in any of those three reference years, assume you''re in Wave 23 unless ZATCA has told you otherwise — direct notification typically arrives around six months ahead, so if you haven''t heard anything and think you should have, it''s worth checking proactively rather than waiting for a letter that may already be delayed.</p>' WHERE story_id = '2026-03-01-saudi-arabia-zatca-wave-23' AND lang = 'en';
UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇨🇱 Chile — digital delivery required without a printer</h3><p>Businesses without point-of-sale printing capability must now deliver the <em>boleta electrónica</em> digitally — by email, SMS, WhatsApp, QR code, or an equivalent electronic channel — rather than simply skipping delivery. A small rule, but one that closes a real gap for mobile vendors, pop-ups, and delivery-only operations that previously had no clearly compliant path when they lacked a physical printer.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you run any point-of-sale operation without a physical printer — markets, pop-ups, delivery-only setups — confirm you actually have one of these electronic channels working today, not just planned for later. Businesses that do have printers must generally still deliver the printed representation as before.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-03-01-chile-digital-boleta-delivery';
UPDATE story_translations SET html = '<h3>🇨🇱 Chile — digital delivery required without a printer</h3><p>Businesses without point-of-sale printing capability must now deliver the <em>boleta electrónica</em> digitally — by email, SMS, WhatsApp, QR code, or an equivalent electronic channel — rather than simply skipping delivery. A small rule, but one that closes a real gap for mobile vendors, pop-ups, and delivery-only operations that previously had no clearly compliant path when they lacked a physical printer.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you run any point-of-sale operation without a physical printer — markets, pop-ups, delivery-only setups — confirm you actually have one of these electronic channels working today, not just planned for later. Businesses that do have printers must generally still deliver the printed representation as before.</p>' WHERE story_id = '2026-03-01-chile-digital-boleta-delivery' AND lang = 'en';
UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇵🇱 Poland — KSeF mandate goes universal</h3><p>From today, Poland''s KSeF requirement extends to essentially every remaining VAT-registered business (micro-entrepreneurs are still on a separate track, joining from January 2027). From this date, an invoice only carries legal force once KSeF has cleared it — and the old-style correction notes (<em>noty korygujące</em>) are no longer valid at all; corrections now have to go through KSeF''s own structured correction process.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you have any Polish B2B invoicing flow that was previously exempt, confirm your system is actually generating valid FA(3) structured invoices now, not just planning to by year-end. Also worth double-checking: from 1 August 2026, KSeF invoice numbers need to appear on bank transfer references too — a small detail that''s easy for a treasury team to miss if they weren''t looped into the e-invoicing rollout.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-04-01-poland-ksef-universal';
UPDATE story_translations SET html = '<h3>🇵🇱 Poland — KSeF mandate goes universal</h3><p>From today, Poland''s KSeF requirement extends to essentially every remaining VAT-registered business (micro-entrepreneurs are still on a separate track, joining from January 2027). From this date, an invoice only carries legal force once KSeF has cleared it — and the old-style correction notes (<em>noty korygujące</em>) are no longer valid at all; corrections now have to go through KSeF''s own structured correction process.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you have any Polish B2B invoicing flow that was previously exempt, confirm your system is actually generating valid FA(3) structured invoices now, not just planning to by year-end. Also worth double-checking: from 1 August 2026, KSeF invoice numbers need to appear on bank transfer references too — a small detail that''s easy for a treasury team to miss if they weren''t looped into the e-invoicing rollout.</p>' WHERE story_id = '2026-04-01-poland-ksef-universal' AND lang = 'en';
UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇧🇷 Brazil — CBS/IBS validation begins</h3><p>As Brazil''s dual-VAT reform progresses, authorization systems started rigorously validating the new CBS and IBS tax fields on NF-e, NFC-e, and NFS-e documents today. Invoices with missing or inconsistent data now risk automatic rejection — still at test rates (0.9% / 0.1%), so no financial impact yet, but a rejected invoice can still hold up the movement of goods regardless of the rate being nominal.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you haven''t already, audit your invoice output for complete CBS/IBS/IS data groups now, while the stakes are still low — waiting until the rates go fully live in August, per Technical Note 2025.002-RTC, is cutting it close.</p><p style="color:#7a6f52; font-size:12.5px; margin-top:20px;">Full technical detail on both of these lives in their respective Deep Dives — Poland and Brazil — if you need the complete picture for a briefing.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-04-01-brazil-cbs-ibs-validation';
UPDATE story_translations SET html = '<h3>🇧🇷 Brazil — CBS/IBS validation begins</h3><p>As Brazil''s dual-VAT reform progresses, authorization systems started rigorously validating the new CBS and IBS tax fields on NF-e, NFC-e, and NFS-e documents today. Invoices with missing or inconsistent data now risk automatic rejection — still at test rates (0.9% / 0.1%), so no financial impact yet, but a rejected invoice can still hold up the movement of goods regardless of the rate being nominal.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you haven''t already, audit your invoice output for complete CBS/IBS/IS data groups now, while the stakes are still low — waiting until the rates go fully live in August, per Technical Note 2025.002-RTC, is cutting it close.</p><p style="color:#7a6f52; font-size:12.5px; margin-top:20px;">Full technical detail on both of these lives in their respective Deep Dives — Poland and Brazil — if you need the complete picture for a briefing.</p>' WHERE story_id = '2026-04-01-brazil-cbs-ibs-validation' AND lang = 'en';
UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇸🇰 Slovakia — voluntary transition period begins</h3><p>Businesses can now register to voluntarily test structured e-invoicing and reporting ahead of Slovakia''s January 2027 mandate, using the country''s distinctive decentralised "5-corner" model built on certified <em>Digital Postman</em> access points running over Peppol — a variant we don''t see replicated exactly anywhere else we track.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you trade with Slovak VAT taxpayers, this is genuinely worth doing early rather than waiting. From 2027, input VAT deductions can''t be claimed on non-compliant incoming invoices — a real cash-flow consequence, not just a paperwork one. Testing now, while there''s no penalty for getting it wrong, is the cheap way to find integration problems before they cost you money.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-05-01-slovakia-voluntary-testing';
UPDATE story_translations SET html = '<h3>🇸🇰 Slovakia — voluntary transition period begins</h3><p>Businesses can now register to voluntarily test structured e-invoicing and reporting ahead of Slovakia''s January 2027 mandate, using the country''s distinctive decentralised "5-corner" model built on certified <em>Digital Postman</em> access points running over Peppol — a variant we don''t see replicated exactly anywhere else we track.</p><p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you trade with Slovak VAT taxpayers, this is genuinely worth doing early rather than waiting. From 2027, input VAT deductions can''t be claimed on non-compliant incoming invoices — a real cash-flow consequence, not just a paperwork one. Testing now, while there''s no penalty for getting it wrong, is the cheap way to find integration problems before they cost you money.</p>' WHERE story_id = '2026-05-01-slovakia-voluntary-testing' AND lang = 'en';
UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇦🇺 Australia — 30% Peppol threshold for federal invoices</h3><p>From 1 July, Non-Corporate Commonwealth Entities must have at least 30% of received supplier invoices flowing through the Peppol network, on the way to full automation by December, with quarterly progress reporting to the Australian Peppol Authority. If you supply Australian federal agencies, this is a good moment to confirm your invoicing is actually Peppol-enabled using the PINT A-NZ format — the only standard supported since May 2025 — not just technically capable of it.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-06-01-australia-peppol-threshold-preview';
UPDATE story_translations SET html = '<h3>🇦🇺 Australia — 30% Peppol threshold for federal invoices</h3><p>From 1 July, Non-Corporate Commonwealth Entities must have at least 30% of received supplier invoices flowing through the Peppol network, on the way to full automation by December, with quarterly progress reporting to the Australian Peppol Authority. If you supply Australian federal agencies, this is a good moment to confirm your invoicing is actually Peppol-enabled using the PINT A-NZ format — the only standard supported since May 2025 — not just technically capable of it.</p>' WHERE story_id = '2026-06-01-australia-peppol-threshold-preview' AND lang = 'en';
UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇩🇰 Denmark — small businesses on custom systems join the mandate</h3><p>Small businesses and sole proprietorships exceeding DKK 300,000 turnover in two consecutive years, using non-registered ("custom") accounting systems, become fully subject to the Bookkeeping Act''s digital requirements. Worth checking whether your turnover has actually crossed that threshold in the last two fiscal years — it''s easy to assume you''re still under it without actually checking the numbers.</p>' WHERE id = '2026-06-01-denmark-small-business-bookkeeping-preview';
