<p>That distinction matters: the legal deadline itself is not moving, only the posture around enforcing it. Invoices received by PDF, email, or paper after 1 September will remain valid, payable, and VAT-deductible for businesses that can show genuine, documented difficulty and active progress toward compliance — this is not a blanket grace period, and the DGFiP has published a practical 29-question guide setting out exactly what "actively progressing" is expected to look like in practice, rather than leaving it to interpretation.</p>
