UPDATE stories SET html_en = '<h3>🇫🇷 France''s e-invoicing readiness numbers, with 50 days to go</h3>
<p>The DGFiP and AIFE, who have run the PPF pilot since February, have shared fresh platform and onboarding figures, and they paint a sobering picture of how much ground is left to cover. Of close to 150 Plateformes Agréées now registered, only around 25 are currently active in actually transmitting data through the system — the rest are accredited but not yet genuinely moving live invoices.</p>
<p>Company-side participation looks thinner still: just 3,800 entities have issued e-invoices and 3,400 have received them through the pilot to date, against a total of more than 11 million entities eventually in scope — a participation rate of roughly 0.025%. Most strikingly, among the exact group facing an immediate issuance obligation from 1 September — large enterprises and mid-sized companies (ETIs) — only 9 Large companies and 37 Mid-sized companies have issued a single invoice through the pilot so far.</p>
<p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you''re a Large or ETI business with an issuance obligation from day one, these figures are a useful reality check — the overwhelming majority of your peer group hasn''t validated their own flow yet either, so don''t assume the wider market is quietly ahead of where you are. Combined with the fact that some technical guidelines and legislative texts are still pending finalisation ahead of a public consultation window, this is genuinely not the moment to treat pilot testing as optional or routine.</p>
' WHERE id = '2026-07-28-france-readiness-numbers';
